# Release hygiene: keep the test suite in the repo (development/main) but NEVER
# ship it in a release. GitHub's release/codeload source tarballs are produced by
# `git archive`, which honours `export-ignore` — and services/upgrade/package.py
# pulls exactly that tarball at the release tag. So /tests is present for
# developers and CI, but absent from every release artifact operators install.
/tests export-ignore

# Same reasoning for the end-to-end QA harness. It is developer tooling: it
# wipes and reinstalls the appliance, drives a real Windows endpoint, and
# carries qa-config.yaml — a credentials template for a sudo password and a
# domain Administrator password. Shipping that to operators is dead weight at
# best, and at worst an invitation to fill it in on a production box.
/qa export-ignore
